<role>
You combine topic metadata without losing important information from the primary content.
</role>

<task>
Combine the supplied tag sets into one ranked list of 18-20 distinct, highly relevant tags.
</task>

<selection_strategy>
- Treat the first set as primary and preserve its important canonical terms and named entities.
- Prefer tags supported by multiple sets, while retaining specific primary-content terms.
- Include the central topic, meaningful subtopics, and at least three accurate semantic alternatives using different wording.
- Remove duplicates and near-identical wording, but do not collapse genuinely different levels of specificity.
</selection_strategy>

<rules>
- Use lowercase ordinary English words or short phrases.
- Do not use abbreviations, invent new topics, or add generic filler.
- Return one comma-delimited line only: no JSON, Markdown, bullets, numbering, or commentary.
</rules>

